; --- the QR login screen (30-39) ---------------------------------------------
MSG_QR_STEP1 (30//)
1. Open Telegram on your phone
MSG_QR_STEP2 (31//)
2. Settings > Devices > Link Desktop Device
MSG_QR_STEP3 (32//)
3. Point the phone at this code
MSG_QR_KEYS (33//)
P: log in with your phone number   ESC quits
MSG_QR_SCAN (34//)
Scan it with Telegram on your phone
;
; --- Log out (40-49) ---------------------------------------------------------
MSG_LOGOUT_TITLE (40//)
Log out
MSG_LOGOUT_BODY (41//)
Log out of Telegram on this computer?\n\n\
Amigram ends this session at Telegram and removes what\n\
it keeps of the account here: telegram-auth.bin, the chat\n\
list, hidden chats, avatars and cached photos. Downloads\n\
and settings stay.\n\n\
Then it quits, and the next start shows the login.
MSG_LOGOUT_BUTTONS (42//)
Log out|Cancel
MSG_LOGOUT_OFFLINE_BODY (43//)
Telegram could not be reached, so the session could\n\
not be ended there.\n\n\
Remove what Amigram keeps of the account on this\n\
computer anyway? The session stays in Telegram's list\n\
of devices (Settings > Devices on your phone) until\n\
you end it there.
MSG_LOGOUT_OFFLINE_BUTTONS (44//)
Remove here|Cancel
MSG_LOGOUT_NOT_LOGGED_IN (45//)
Not logged in yet
MSG_LOGOUT_LOGGING_OUT (46//)
Logging out...
MSG_LOGOUT_FAILED (47//)
Log out failed: Telegram not reached
;
; --- the update (50-59) ------------------------------------------------------
MSG_UPDATE_TITLE (50//)
Update
MSG_UPDATE_OFFER (51//)
Amigram %s is out: you have %s.\n\n\
Update now? Amigram fetches it from the channel\n\
@%s, checks that its author signed it and\n\
keeps this version as Amigram.old.
MSG_UPDATE_BUTTONS (52//)
Update|Later
MSG_UPDATE_FETCHING (53//)
Fetching Amigram %s...
MSG_UPDATE_INSTALLED (54//)
Amigram %s is installed.\n\n\
Quit now and start Amigram again to use it.\n\
The old version is kept as Amigram.old.
MSG_UPDATE_INSTALLED_BUTTONS (55//)
Quit|Later
MSG_UPDATE_INSTALLED_STATUS (56//)
Amigram %s installed: start it again
MSG_UPDATE_FAILED (57//)
The update failed
